{"archetypes":[{"name":"batch-schema-fit","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan registers breadcrumbs/ in larch-log-batches.sh as a 'sanitizer-required batch' AND adds a direct directory-walker in larch-log.sh — but the existing batch table schema (4-column: slug .ext mode sanitizer) maps fixed slugs to single named files, not to directories of dynamically-named per-PID files; the two mechanisms may be redundant, conflicting, or the batch entry may be dead code that never gets dispatched.","prompt_body":"Read scripts/larch-log-batches.sh in full and note the 4-column batch table format (slug .ext mode sanitizer) — every existing entry maps a fixed slug to a single file path. Then read scripts/larch-log.sh to see how it dispatches writes: confirm whether the write/append commands consume larch_log_batch_list to iterate or only accept explicit --batch arguments from callers. Determine whether the table schema can accommodate a directory of dynamically-named files (breadcrumbs/collect-agent-results.<pid>.ndjson, etc.) or whether only fixed-slug→fixed-file mappings are supported. Flag any scenario where adding a breadcrumbs batch entry to the table would either be dead code (larch-log.sh never dispatches it autonomously) or would conflict with the plan's separate direct-walker implementation in larch-log.sh. If both mechanisms are real, identify which is authoritative and whether the plan must extend the batch schema or remove one mechanism. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"category-routing-coherence","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan states a general emoji-prefix routing rule (⚠/❌→warn, →→progress) but then overrides it for specific ci-wait.sh callsites — line 282 '⚠ suspend detected' is assigned wait-ci not warn, and line 255 '⚠ Bailing' stays on larch_err — creating silent exceptions that contradict the stated rule and will confuse reviewers and future editors.","prompt_body":"Read scripts/lib-quiet.sh to confirm the exact category vocabulary enforced by larch_quiet_bc_valid_category() (lines ~129-131). Then read the ci-wait.sh routing decisions in the plan: line 282 has an ⚠ prefix but the plan assigns --category=wait-ci rather than warn; line 255 has ⚠ Bailing and stays on larch_err rather than becoming emit_breadcrumb at all. Check whether these exceptions are internally consistent with each other and with the stated emoji-prefix rule. For the other four files (ship-pr.sh, review-and-fix.sh, review-core.sh, collect-agent-results.sh, dispatch-panel.sh), verify the plan's stated routing rule for no-emoji free-form callsites (default to progress) against any callsites whose text content implies an error or warning state — a blanket progress default on error-text callsites would mislabel failure events in the stream. Verify every category the plan assigns (progress, warn, stall, retry, escalate, wait-ci, network-flake) is present in the larch_quiet_bc_valid_category case statement. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"stale-line-targets","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan assigns specific line numbers to every ci-wait.sh larch_errf callsite (184, 191, 207, 222, 238, 249, 251, 253, 255, 257, 268, 271, 282) and claims a total of 50 callsites across 5 named files; if any line numbers have drifted since the plan was authored the implementer will edit wrong lines or miss callsites.","prompt_body":"Read scripts/ci-wait.sh fully and list every larch_errf and emit_breadcrumb callsite with its actual current line number; compare against the plan's enumeration (184, 191, 207, 222, 238, 249, 251, 253, 255, 257, 268, 271, 282) and report any line-number drift or missing/extra callsites. Then grep for emit_breadcrumb in scripts/ship-pr.sh, skills/review-and-fix/scripts/review-and-fix.sh, skills/review/scripts/review-core.sh, scripts/collect-agent-results.sh, and skills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh and verify the plan's claim of exactly 23+20+4+2+1=50 total callsites; report any discrepancy. If any callsite in ci-wait.sh is already an emit_breadcrumb call (meaning item-2 work is partially done), note it so the plan's scope claim is accurate. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
